think Continued the autonomous Season G font run after the circumflex lap sent clean. The prior lap named the German eszett as the remaining accented-coverage rung. Chose to widen it into a coherent German-letters corpus rather than a lone eszett: the a umlaut and o umlaut are also undrawn (only the u umlaut lives in the acute/cedilla corpus), so ä, ö, and ß together complete a German keeper's name -- Muller, Schafer, Weiss -- a stronger Lindy lap than one glyph alone. Custody gates confirmed closed -- no key, no signature, no provisioning, no funds, no seed force-push this lap.
think Council rota by lap index: cycling forward from item 24, this lap's slot is item 25 -- active-designing/20260816-205859_double-seat-expansion-eight-seasons.md, deep-read in full at the start of this session's run. Season G names the open-media family (image, sound, fonts, video, terminal, text); this corpus fills its font strand.
think Designed the crux as UMLAUT-VERSUS-LETTERFORM, distinct from the accent-lean proofs. The umlaut is two SEPARATED dots -- top-row ink at columns 1 and 3 with the center column empty between them, the same two-dot mark the existing u umlaut carries. The eszett is a LETTER, not a mark -- a full-height letterform whose top is a joined curve with ink on the center column where an umlaut leaves a gap. So the proof reads the top row and tells a dotted vowel from a full letter by whether the center column is a gap or a join.
think Drew the two umlaut vowels by reusing the acute/grave/circumflex vowel bodies (rows 2-6) under the two-dot umlaut on row 0, matching the existing u umlaut exactly. Drew the eszett as a left-stem letterform with an upper and lower bowl and a joined top (row0 .##.., col 2 inked). Guards written atomic: UmlautLeftDotMissing, UmlautRightDotMissing, UmlautDotsMerged (center must be empty), EszettMissingJoinedTop (center must be inked) -- four toothed guards, no compound assert.
think Hand-computed ink counts before running: eszett 15, a umlaut 16, o umlaut 14 -- band lo 14, hi 16, inside the honest [12,18]. Codepoints strictly ascending 0xDF,0xE4,0xF6 (the eszett sorts first, below the umlaut vowels), count 3, last o umlaut U+00F6.
obs GREEN on the first metal run, no red: ink band 14..16 exactly as hand-computed, encoded 143 bytes over raw 105, all three present/distinct/legible, the two umlauts two-dotted with a center gap and the eszett a joined letterform. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, both files plain 7-bit ASCII though the glyphs cover a non-ASCII range (the ascii-first font-codec exception).
obs Pure additive font content -- a fresh module and witness; the accent trio and every sibling stand untouched. No network, no key, no funds; no custody gate reached. With the u umlaut already in the acute/cedilla corpus, the accented Latin-1 vowel set is now whole across all three leans (acute, grave, circumflex) plus the umlauts and the eszett -- a device can spell Romance, French, Italian, Portuguese, and German keeper names.
loom witness=font5x7_german_witness glyphs=3 cell=5x7 encoded_bytes=143 raw_bytes=105 ink_lo=14 ink_hi=16
